cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use DeepQMC for your work, please cite the preferred citation below.
  If your work involves excited-state optimization or geometrically
  transferable training specifically, please also cite the corresponding
  paper listed under "references".
title: DeepQMC
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jan
    family-names: Hermann
  - given-names: Zeno
    family-names: Schätzle
    email: zeno.schaetzle@fu-berlin.de
  - given-names: Péter Bernát
    family-names: Szabó
    email: peter.bernat.szabo@fu-berlin.de
  - given-names: M.
    family-names: Mezera
  - name: DeepQMC Contributors
repository-code: https://github.com/deepqmc/deepqmc
url: https://deepqmc.github.io
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.3960826
license: MIT
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    DeepQMC: An open-source software suite for variational optimization of
    deep-learning molecular wave functions
  authors:
    - given-names: Zeno
      family-names: Schätzle
    - given-names: Péter Bernát
      family-names: Szabó
    - given-names: M.
      family-names: Mezera
    - given-names: Jan
      family-names: Hermann
    - given-names: Frank
      family-names: Noé
  journal: The Journal of Chemical Physics
  volume: 159
  issue: 9
  start: "094108"
  year: 2023
  month: 9
  doi: 10.1063/5.0157512
  url: https://doi.org/10.1063/5.0157512
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      An Improved Penalty-Based Excited-State Variational Monte Carlo
      Approach with Deep-Learning Ansatzes
    authors:
      - given-names: Péter Bernát
        family-names: Szabó
      - given-names: Zeno
        family-names: Schätzle
      - given-names: M.
        family-names: Entwistle
      - given-names: Frank
        family-names: Noé
    journal: Journal of Chemical Theory and Computation
    year: 2024
    month: 8
    doi: 10.1021/acs.jctc.4c00678
    url: https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.4c00678
    notes: Cite this when using the excited-state optimization approach.
  - type: unpublished
    title: >-
      Ab-Initio Simulation of Excited-State Potential Energy Surfaces with
      Transferable Deep Quantum Monte Carlo
    authors:
      - given-names: Zeno
        family-names: Schätzle
      - given-names: Péter Bernát
        family-names: Szabó
      - given-names: A.
        family-names: Cuzzocrea
      - given-names: Frank
        family-names: Noé
    year: 2025
    month: 3
    doi: 10.48550/arXiv.2503.19847
    url: https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2503.19847
    notes: >-
      Cite this when using geometrically transferable training on a fixed
      set of molecular configurations, the dynamic overlap penalty, or
      non-adiabatic coupling calculations.
  - type: unpublished
    title: >-
      Enabling ab initio geometry optimization of strongly correlated
      systems with transferable deep quantum Monte Carlo
    authors:
      - given-names: Péter Bernát
        family-names: Szabó
      - given-names: Zeno
        family-names: Schätzle
      - given-names: Frank
        family-names: Noé
    year: 2026
    doi: 10.48550/arXiv.2603.25381
    url: https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2603.25381
    notes: >-
      Cite this when using continuous transferable simulation of potential
      energy surfaces via dynamic nuclear geometry sampling, e.g. for ab
      initio geometry optimization.
